From: tj-barrett <barrett.t@northeastern.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] pastix.c: refactorize before giving up when a reused LU fails

Between Newton iterations ccx's PaStiX interface reuses the LU factorization of an
earlier matrix as a preconditioner for GMRES (IPARM_REUSE_LU). If GMRES does not
converge in double precision with diagonal scaling already off, ccx exited with
status 5 -- without ever factorizing the current matrix. With a viscoelastic UMAT
(30 increments, ~100 solves) GMRES regularly needed its full 70 iterations, and a
run on two GPUs (different task scheduling) stopped at 3.8e-12 against the 1e-12
target and exited.

Record whether the current call factorized the matrix or reused an earlier LU, and
in the latter case refactorize and solve again before giving up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/ccx_2.23/src/pastix.c
+++ b/ccx_2.23/src/pastix.c
@@ -1094,6 +1094,10 @@
         }
     }
 
+	// remember whether this call factorizes the current matrix or reuses an
+	// earlier factorization (IPARM_REUSE_LU) as a preconditioner for GMRES
+	char freshFactor = forceRedo;
+
 	//invoke init
 	pastix_init(ad,au,adb,aub,sigma,icol,irow, 
 		 neq,nzs,symmetryflag,inputformat,jq,nzs3);
@@ -1114,6 +1118,17 @@
 		
 		// Give up, if we tried it with double precision, use backup b otherwise
 		if(globDoublePrecision == 1 && noScale ){
+            if( !freshFactor ){
+                // The factorization was reused from an earlier matrix and is too
+                // poor a preconditioner for this one: factorize the current matrix
+                // before giving up (previously ccx exited here)
+                memcpy(b, b_backup, sizeof(double) * (*nrhs)*(*neq));
+                printf("refactorizing: the reused factorization did not converge\n");
+                forceRedo = 1;
+                pastix_main_generic(ad, au, adb, aub, sigma, b, icol, irow, neq, nzs, symmetryflag, inputformat, jq, nzs3, nrhs);
+                SFREE(b_backup);
+                return;
+            }
             printf("PaStiX could not converge to a valid result\n");
             exit(5);
         }
